  "notes": "quote_asset_precision added 2026-09-07 (cf-arb-bot-review-plan.md Tier 1 step 1.3) -- re-verified live against exchangeInfo. All other fields already matched the live venue; only the price-side precision was previously missing. order_types is unchanged and confirmed live: NONE of these 9 symbols advertise IMMEDIATE_OR_CANCEL or FILL_OR_KILL support -- only LIMIT/MARKET/LIMIT_MAKER. MEXC's order-type ENUM (see spot_v3 docs, 'Order type') does include IMMEDIATE_OR_CANCEL and FILL_OR_KILL as values, and there is no separate timeInForce parameter on POST /api/v3/order -- the type value itself carries that semantic. But exchangeInfo's per-symbol order_types is what the venue actually accepts for a given symbol, and it excludes both here. This is the wire-format problem the independent review flagged: an executor that submits type=IOC (not even a real value) or type=IMMEDIATE_OR_CANCEL against these symbols is submitting a request the venue's own published capability data says it will reject. Fixed by making order-type configurable and startup-validating it against this file per symbol (fail closed in live mode) rather than resolving the underlying strategy question here -- that requires either a live authenticated probe (blocked: no MEXC_API_KEY/MEXC_API_SECRET in this environment, and CLAUDE.md #9/#8 forbid trusting an unverified channel or hitting a live exchange from an automated path) or a redesign around a resting LIMIT/LIMIT_MAKER order, which is out of this plan's scope.",
